134
00:25:21.690 --> 00:25:28.170
Nana Essilfie-Conduah: hedera is an evm equivalent network. And on ethereum and other evm networks there isn't this

135
00:25:28.290 --> 00:25:50.040
Nana Essilfie-Conduah: big issue of sort of like transaction size limits. Right? It's it's mostly governed by the available gas in a block and a user's ability to pay on Hiro. However, there's a 6 kB transaction size limit. If you include signatures as well. That limits how big a transaction can get. And this is a very deep or foundational architectural decision.

136
00:25:50.545 --> 00:25:56.580
Nana Essilfie-Conduah: To get around this when you're creating smart contracts that are larger than this size in hip

137
00:25:56.730 --> 00:26:03.980
Nana Essilfie-Conduah: 4, 10. This was back in 2022, the network added the ability to temporarily use the

138
00:26:04.020 --> 00:26:21.629
Nana Essilfie-Conduah: hedera, or now now the Hiro file service to temporarily hold byte code that was larger than this size, and then, at the time of execution, the Evm. The smart contract process would be able to pick up that byte code that was larger than the 6 kB and process it. So that's the context.

139
00:26:21.650 --> 00:26:37.200
Nana Essilfie-Conduah: the issue there is that when you have large contracts larger than this size, the 6 kB, what happens is that the relay operator, like, you know, the person running the Rpc. Or the person submitting the ethereum transaction to the network

140
00:26:37.320 --> 00:26:48.059
Nana Essilfie-Conduah: has to separately use the file service to create these transactions. And it could be N number of transactions. The file create. And you know, multiple file appends depending on how big the size is

141
00:26:48.200 --> 00:27:12.249
Nana Essilfie-Conduah: the relay operator end up ends up having to cover that cost right? This is an extra business cost that is very unique to Hiro. So people that run, you know, if you took inferior, or if you took alchemy, let's say 3rd web. Some of the people running Rpcs on on Hedera. They don't have the same cost in other evm networks, so on, on hedera or on Hiro.

142
00:27:12.400 --> 00:27:18.839
Nana Essilfie-Conduah: they have to pay an extra amount every time a user submits a large contract execution.

